      <div class="lp-two-col">
        <div class="lp-prose">
          <p>La Grange's 1900s–1950s Craftsman bungalows, Georgian colonials, and commercial facades used lime putty and natural cement mortars that require expert matching. Pre-war buildings need lime putty; post-war need Portland blends. Applying Portland to pre-war brick — the most common contractor error — causes irreversible spalling. We serve zip codes {zipCodes} across Cook County.</p>
          <p>Downtown La Grange commercial facades show decades of mixed repair mortar from different contractors — visual inconsistency and structural gaps throughout. Our commercial assessment identifies original vs. repair mortar and develops a protocol for full consistency. Free estimates, written scope, historic brick handled correctly.</p>
